      "content": "Hey, I'm prepping a keynote for the upcoming trade summit in Jakarta. I really want to connect with the local delegates and avoid sounding like some stiff Westerner. I found this phrase online: \"Makan hati.\" I was thinking of working it into my opening remarks to show I've done my homework. Is that a safe, neutral phrase to use to show rapport, or is it risky?",
